n't tell left from right); four eyespots on the diagonals. Each oar rows only while it points within ~80° of DOWN (its statolith above 60% or below 40%), so whatever way up the cell is, the oars underneath push it up: it has no right way up and climbs from the floor lying any way (Saltella can't). Each stroke twists the body, so it doesn't swim straight: it cartwheels (~20°/s), handing the job from oar to oar. Oars row while no eyespot sees more than 25% sun and one sees more than 1.5%; it rests when all see less than 1%. Its day: rolls up from the depths at dawn (~9 µm/s), rides 700-900 µm, chases the dusk light to ~400 µm, rests and sinks to ~1.7 mm by dawn (off the surface at night). Measured from the floor at any angle: 3 days, never starving, starch full by mid-afternoon. Uses 11 brain slots (needs the 16-slot nucleus).","design":{"body":{"radius":10},"parts":[{"type":"sensor","id":"eyeFL","label":"Light sensor","at":[7.0710678118654755,7.071067811865475],"angle":45,"kind":"light","cone":180,"build":{"tpl":"Light sensor (eyespot)","where":45,"tilt":0,"size":1,"depth":1,"feels":"strangers","flip":false,"id":"eyeFL"},"name":"Eyespot (front-left)"},{"type":"sensor","id":"eyeBL","label":"Light sensor","at":[-7.071067811865475,7.0710678118654755],"angle":135,"kind":"light","cone":180,"build":{"tpl":"Light sensor (eyespot)","where":135,"tilt":0,"size":1,"depth":1,"feels":"strangers","flip":false,"id":"eyeBL"},"name":"Eyespot (back-left)"},{"type":"sensor","id":"eyeBR","label":"Light sensor","at":[-7.071067811865477,-7.071067811865475],"angle":225,"kind":"light","cone":180,"build":{"tpl":"Light sensor (eyespot)","where":225,"tilt":0,"size":1,"depth":1,"feels":"strangers","flip":false,"id":"eyeBR"},"name":"Eyespot (back-right)"},{"type":"sensor","id":"eyeFR","label":"Light sensor","at":[7.071067811865474,-7.071067811865477],"angle":315,"kind":"light","cone":180,"build":{"tpl":"Light sensor (eyespot)","where":315,"tilt":0,"size":1,"depth":1,"feels":"strangers","flip":fa